Qwen3.5-35B-A3B thin bundle for Tenstorrent Blackhole

This bundle contains no model weights and no container image.

The model, Qwen/Qwen3.5-35B-A3B, is by the Qwen team (Alibaba Cloud) and is licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (see LICENSE, copied
from the model repository at revision 59d61f3ce65a6d9863b86d2e96597125219dc754). The weights are fetched from the Hugging Face Hub at that
revision when the server first starts.

The wheels in wheels/ were built from tt-metal (Apache License 2.0) as it is installed in the Tenstorrent image
tt-model/qwen3-coder-next:0c170421ca1b, the image of the raahemnabeel/qwen3-coder-next bundle:
  - ttnn: the image's tt-metal build, packaged with the image's own setup.py. It includes the image's SFPI compiler (a Tenstorrent build of
    GCC for the RISC-V cores, version 7.74.0, under runtime/sfpi); its source is at https://github.com/tenstorrent/sfpi and it keeps its
    own licenses;
  - tt_metal_models: the image's `models` tree. One file, models/autoports/qwen_qwen3_coder_next/tt/weights.py, has the 41-line patch of
    the recipe package qwen3.5-35b-a3b-blackhole-p300 applied. The patch adds a reader for this checkpoint's tensor layout;
  - vllm_tt_plugin: the vLLM plugin installed in that image.
config.json in base_config/ is the model repository's config.json with three edits (the architecture name, no multi-token-prediction
layers, no mrope keys).
